      "answer": "IVMS (In-Vehicle Monitoring System) is part of the vehicle telematics offerings, including OLIWA and iVMS-PLUS. It focuses on stable tracking, compliance, and report readiness. The baseline configuration for IVMS includes creating or verifying units, ensuring correct tracker model mapping, and applying baseline alerts such as overspeed, ignition on/off, geofence in/out, and towing (if supported). It also involves applying baseline reports like daily trips, stops, mileage, and driver behavior summaries if ECO/DSC is enabled.\n\nSource: NAVAS CMS User Manual — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
